    "Two staff members of Doctors Without Borders were killed during an Israeli airstrike on a Gaza City clinic.",
    "The medical organization stated the clinic's location was known to the Israeli military and clearly marked.",
    "The Israeli military alleged that the two deceased individuals were affiliated with Hamas as terrorists."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The incident occurred in Gaza City when an Israeli airstrike hit a facility operated by the international medical aid group Doctors Without Borders, also known as Médecins Sans Frontières. The organization confirmed the deaths of two of its staff members during the strike, noting that the clinic was a known, marked location. Following the event, the World Health Organization and other international observers expressed strong condemnation of the military action. In response to the claims, the Israeli military asserted that the two individuals killed were combatants linked to Hamas, characterizing them as terrorists. This event is part of broader ongoing military activity in the region, which has recently included strikes targeting other Hamas-affiliated figures and their families, as reported by various international news outlets during the same period.",
